\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces A coherent state $\mathinner {|{\alpha }\delimiter "526930B }$, enters port $a$ of a beam splitter. A signal $\mathinner {|{\Psi }\delimiter "526930B }$ enters port $b$. These two beams interfere, resulting in photons being detected at the $c$ and $d$ ports. The two photo-currents are subtracted, and the signal that is produced is proportional to an arbitrary quadrature of the state $\mathinner {|{\Psi }\delimiter "526930B }$. The quadrature that is measured is determined by the homodyne angle, $\phi $. This is expressed mathematically by Equation (\ref  {eq:BHD_for_ligo_general_quadrature}).\relax }}{39}{figure.caption.44}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbhdsketch}{{5.1}{39}{A coherent state $\ket {\alpha }$, enters port $a$ of a beam splitter. A signal $\ket {\Psi }$ enters port $b$. These two beams interfere, resulting in photons being detected at the $c$ and $d$ ports. The two photo-currents are subtracted, and the signal that is produced is proportional to an arbitrary quadrature of the state $\ket {\Psi }$. The quadrature that is measured is determined by the homodyne angle, $\phi $. This is expressed mathematically by Equation (\ref {eq:BHD_for_ligo_general_quadrature}).\relax }{figure.caption.44}{}}
