\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The intensity noise of the light at the AS port for the A+ detector. This was obtained by deconvolving the detectors sensitivity curve with the function shown in Figure \ref  {fig:bhdforligochapterdetectorrepsonse}. At frequencies above 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz the noise is flat as it is dominated by shot noise. At lower frequencies the noise is increased relative to shot noise due to radiation pressure, coating thermal noise and other noise sources. The spike in the spectrum at 500Hz represents the presence of suspension modes (\leavevmode {\color {red}actually find out what this is}). \relax }}{49}{figure.caption.59}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterlightnoise}{{5.4}{49}{The intensity noise of the light at the AS port for the A+ detector. This was obtained by deconvolving the detectors sensitivity curve with the function shown in Figure \ref {fig:bhdforligochapterdetectorrepsonse}. At frequencies above 1\,kHz the noise is flat as it is dominated by shot noise. At lower frequencies the noise is increased relative to shot noise due to radiation pressure, coating thermal noise and other noise sources. The spike in the spectrum at 500Hz represents the presence of suspension modes (\textcolor {red}{actually find out what this is}). \relax }{figure.caption.59}{}}
