\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbeamshape}{{6.3}{61}{The top panel shows the radius of the beam as it travels from the SRM (z = 0) to the waist of the OMC. Significant points along the axis are marked with vertical lines. Less significant, but useful, reference points are marked by dashed vertical lines. The bottom panel shows the Gouy phase shift accumulated by the beam as it propagates along the optical axis.\relax }{figure.caption.77}{}}
