\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.9}{\ignorespaces Left panel: the dark current for each photodiode at their maximum datasheet specified reverse bias as a function of temperature. The apparatus limited dark current measurements to a couple of nanoamps. Exponentials were fitted to the data. Photodiodes with similar cut-off wavelengths share marker shapes, and 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mm photodiodes have larger markers than the 0.5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mm ones. The measurement of the DC dark current approached the noise floor of the apparatus around a few nanovolts. Right panel: the dark noise of each photodiode was measured as a function of temperature. The black dashed line indicates the shot noise level for a 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mA current. At 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, the measurements for the IG24x500S4i did not change much as the temperature changed, there was a knee around this frequency (see Figure \ref  {fig:pdappendixig24temperaturenoisecurrent}); the noise of the IG24x500S4i was $600-700\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\pico \ampere /\sqrt  {\hertz }}$ at 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz.\relax }}{108}{figure.caption.149}}
\newlabel{fig:pdchapterdarkcurrenttermperaturealldiodes}{{8.9}{108}{Left panel: the dark current for each photodiode at their maximum datasheet specified reverse bias as a function of temperature. The apparatus limited dark current measurements to a couple of nanoamps. Exponentials were fitted to the data. Photodiodes with similar cut-off wavelengths share marker shapes, and 1\,mm photodiodes have larger markers than the 0.5\,mm ones. The measurement of the DC dark current approached the noise floor of the apparatus around a few nanovolts. Right panel: the dark noise of each photodiode was measured as a function of temperature. The black dashed line indicates the shot noise level for a 10\,mA current. At 10\,Hz, the measurements for the IG24x500S4i did not change much as the temperature changed, there was a knee around this frequency (see Figure \ref {fig:pdappendixig24temperaturenoisecurrent}); the noise of the IG24x500S4i was $600-700\,\si {\pico \ampere /\sqrt {\hertz }}$ at 10\,Hz.\relax }{figure.caption.149}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.10}{\ignorespaces The saturation limit of three Laser Components photodiodes was measured. The photodiodes were biased so that their noise at 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz was equal to the shot noise of a 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mA current. The IG24x500S4i and IG26x500S4i were exposed to a beam whose $3\sigma $ width was 220\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\micro \metre } and the IG22x1000S4i was exposed to a beam whose $3\sigma $ width was 1000\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\micro \metre }. The size of the light modulation whose relative size was known was tracked as the DC photocurrent was increased. As the photodiodes saturated, the relative size of the AC signal decreased. These photodiodes had low saturation limits compared to the FD10D, which showed no signs of saturation up to 16.5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mA (see Figure \ref  {fig:pdchapterfd10dacdc}).\relax }}{109}{figure.caption.150}}
\newlabel{fig:pdchapterlasercomponentsratio}{{8.10}{109}{The saturation limit of three Laser Components photodiodes was measured. The photodiodes were biased so that their noise at 10\,Hz was equal to the shot noise of a 10\,mA current. The IG24x500S4i and IG26x500S4i were exposed to a beam whose $3\sigma $ width was 220\,\si {\micro \metre } and the IG22x1000S4i was exposed to a beam whose $3\sigma $ width was 1000\,\si {\micro \metre }. The size of the light modulation whose relative size was known was tracked as the DC photocurrent was increased. As the photodiodes saturated, the relative size of the AC signal decreased. These photodiodes had low saturation limits compared to the FD10D, which showed no signs of saturation up to 16.5\,mA (see Figure \ref {fig:pdchapterfd10dacdc}).\relax }{figure.caption.150}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {8.8}Excess Noise in the Photocurrent made by the IG24x500S4i}{110}{section.8.8}}
