\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.15}{\ignorespaces The P5968 InSb detector had its cathode grounded and the noise of the photocurrent due to the blackbody radiation produced by room temperature aluminium was measured (red). The expected level of photocurrent was calculated to be 5.5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\micro \ampere } and the measured photocurrent was 5.3\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\micro \ampere }. The noise level of the photocurrent corresponds to shot noise (green). The noise of the transimpedance amplifier (blue) is well below the shot noise of the photocurrent.\relax }}{116}{figure.caption.159}}
\newlabel{fig:pdchapterp5968noise}{{8.15}{116}{The P5968 InSb detector had its cathode grounded and the noise of the photocurrent due to the blackbody radiation produced by room temperature aluminium was measured (red). The expected level of photocurrent was calculated to be 5.5\,\si {\micro \ampere } and the measured photocurrent was 5.3\,\si {\micro \ampere }. The noise level of the photocurrent corresponds to shot noise (green). The noise of the transimpedance amplifier (blue) is well below the shot noise of the photocurrent.\relax }{figure.caption.159}{}}
